/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"par":{"close":{"tw":[["closure",4],["end",2],["finish",2],["last",0],["complete",2],["draw",3],["plug",3],["open",1]],"en":"Last winter the town decided on the closure of the small library. Nobody wanted to see it close, but the money had run out. My neighbours signed a paper to ask for a new end date. After months of work we managed to complete the repairs ourselves and finish the roof before the cold came. On the last evening a reporter came to draw a picture of the empty hall. We pulled the plug of the old coffee machine and opened every window to let the dust out. It felt like an open door again.","zh":"去年冬天镇上决定关闭那间小图书馆。没有人想看着它关门，但经费已经用完了。邻居们签了一份请愿书，要求给一个新的截止日期。忙了几个月，我们自己修好了屋顶，赶在寒潮前把工程做完。最后一个晚上，一位记者来画下了空荡荡的大厅。我们拔掉了旧咖啡机的插头，把每扇窗都打开放灰尘出去。它又像一扇开着的门了。"},"climb":{"tw":[["steep",6],["raise",0],["move",2],["grow",2],["jump",3],["ride",3],["rise",2],["peak",6],["mount",0]],"en":"The path to the top is steep, and the last hour of it is a slow climb. We begin early, before the sun can raise the heat of the day. Step by step we move up and watch the farms below grow small. My brother likes to jump from rock to rock, while I prefer to ride the old cable car. Every spring more visitors rise with the first light, so we chose a quiet Tuesday instead. At the peak we mount a small flag on the stone and eat our bread in the wind.","zh":"上山顶的路很陡，最后一段更是一步一步地爬。我们很早就出发，趁太阳还没把热气升起来。一级一级往上走，看着下面的农庄变得越来越小。弟弟喜欢在石头间跳来跳去，我更愿意坐那趟旧缆车。每年春天都有更多游客跟着第一缕光上山，所以我们挑了安静的周二。到了山顶，我们在石头上竖了一面小旗，在风里啃面包。"},"shout":{"tw":[["loud",6],["call",0],["scream",3],["cry",0],["curse",3],["noise",3],["express",2],["whisper",1],["talk",2]],"en":"At the school sports day everybody shouts. My father can shout so loud that his voice carries across the whole field. He will call my name and I run faster. When our team scores, the crowd begins to scream and cry with joy. A few boys curse the referee and make a lot of noise, so a teacher tells them to express their feelings in a better way. My quiet aunt does not shout at all; she can only whisper, yet we still talk for hours. Loud or soft, her words reach me.","zh":"学校运动会那天人人都在喊。我爸喊起来响得能穿过整个操场。他一叫我的名字，我就跑得更快。我们队得分时，全场又尖叫又欢呼。有几个男孩骂裁判、闹得很吵，老师让他们换个方式表达情绪。我那位安静的姑妈从来不喊，她只能小声说话，可我们仍能聊上几个小时。无论是喊出来的还是轻声说的，她的话我都能听见。"},"hide":{"tw":[["cover",3],["change",2],["skin",0],["conceal",0],["find",6],["harbor",3],["earth",3],["reveal",6]],"en":"The little fox knows how to hide. It will cover its body with dry leaves and change the colour of its coat with the seasons. In the cold months its skin turns white, which is the best way to conceal itself on snow. We could not find it for a whole week. One morning, near the harbor, it sat on the black earth beside a boat and looked at us. It had been sleeping under that same boat the whole time. Then it moved, and the light seemed to reveal a thin line of red fur along its back.","zh":"那只小狐狸很会藏。它用干叶子盖住身子，还随季节变换毛色。天冷的那几个月，它的皮毛转成白色，这是雪地里最好的隐藏办法。整整一周我们都没找到它。有天早上，在港口附近，它坐在一条船边的黑土上看着我们。接着它一动，光似乎把背脊上一道细细的红毛露了出来。"},"pull":{"tw":[["draw",3],["push",1],["force",2],["tear",0],["move",6],["bring",3],["drive",2],["catch",3]],"en":"Our old car stopped in the mud after the rain. My brother had to pull the small trailer by hand. He used a rope to draw it forward while I pushed from behind with all my force. The work was slow and I began to tear my jacket on the door. A farmer came over to help, and together we managed to move the trailer to the road. He offered to bring his truck and used his tractor to drive both cars home. We did not want to catch a cold in the rain.","zh":"雨后我们那辆旧车陷在泥里。弟弟只好用手拖那个小挂车。他用绳子往前拉，我在后面使劲推。活儿很慢，我的外套在车门上开始撕开了。一位农夫过来帮忙，我俩一起把挂车挪到了路上。他提出开他的卡车来，最后用拖拉机把两辆车都拖回了家。我们可不想在雨里感上风寒。"},"join":{"tw":[["unite",0],["connect",2],["junction",4],["joiner",4],["fair",3],["close",3],["union",0],["meet",6]],"en":"Two villages decided to join their small schools. The teachers wanted to unite the classes and connect the old halls with a new path. At the junction of the two roads the workers built a wide gate, and a joiner made the wooden doors by hand. The two head teachers meet every Monday to plan the week. On the day of the fair, families from both sides came close to the stage and watched the children sing. The union of two schools was not easy, but now nobody can tell which child came from which side.","zh":"两个村子决定把各自的小学合并。老师们想把班级并在一起，用一条新路把两座旧校舍连起来。在两条路的交叉口，工人们修了一座宽门，一位木匠手工做了那两扇木门。两位校长每周一碰头商量这一周的安排。集市那天，两边的家庭都凑到台前看孩子们唱歌。两校合一并不容易，但现在没人分得清哪个孩子来自哪一边。"},"decide":{"tw":[["decision",4],["settle",0],["determine",2],["judge",3],["decisive",4],["rule",3],["resolve",0],["agree",6]],"en":"Our class had to decide where to spend the last school trip. The teacher said the decision must come from us. First we tried to settle the money problem, because that would determine everything else. Two students wanted the sea and three wanted the hills. We asked our teacher to judge which plan was fair. In the end his most decisive answer was simple: ask more people. When the vote was over we had to rule out the far places and resolve one last question about the bus. Everyone agreed.","zh":"我们班得决定最后一次班级旅行去哪儿。老师说这个决定必须由我们自己来做。我们先想办法解决钱的问题，因为那会决定其他一切。两个同学想去海边，三个想去山里。我们请老师来评判哪个方案更公平。最后他给出的最果断的回答很简单：多问些人。投票结束后，我们只能排除太远的地方，再解决最后一个关于大巴的疑问。所有人都同意了。"},"difference":{"tw":[["different",4],["differ",4],["differentiate",4],["conflict",0],["balance",3],["gap",3],["remainder",0],["quality",2]],"en":"The two reports about the same meeting were very different. They differ on one point only: the cost. Nobody could explain the difference, and soon it turned into a small conflict. My job was to check the balance of the two lists and find the gap between them. The remainder was small, but the quality of the work was not the same at all. In the end we had to differentiate between what we measured and what we guessed. That one difference changed the whole decision, and afterwards the two teams never worked in the same room again.","zh":"同一场会议的两份报告很不一样。它们只在一个点上不同：成本。没人能解释这个差异，很快它就变成了一场小冲突。我的工作是核对两张清单是否平衡，找出它们之间的缺口。剩余的部分很小，但工作的质量完全不同。最后我们不得不区分哪些是我们实测的、哪些是猜的。正是这一个差异改变了整个决定，此后两支队伍再也没在同一间屋里共事过。"},"judge":{"tw":[["judicial",4],["judiciary",4],["adjudicate",4],["guess",0],["decide",2],["try",0],["court",6],["jury",6],["think",2]],"en":"Nobody wanted to judge that case. The judicial system moves slowly here, and the judiciary in our town has only two small rooms. First the jury has to listen to both sides, then the judge has to decide. You cannot guess; you have to try every door and think about what is fair. To adjudicate a case like this takes weeks. Two old men sat at the back of the court all day and said nothing. When the decision finally came, the judge wrote three long pages, and everybody went home tired.","zh":"没人愿意审那个案子。这里的司法体系走得很慢，我们镇上的司法部门只有两间小屋。首先要由陪审团听双方陈述，然后由法官作出裁决。你不能靠猜，必须试遍每一条门路，想清楚什么是公平的。裁决这样一个案子要好几周。两个老人整天坐在法庭后排，一言不发。裁决终于下来时，法官写了三页长文，所有人都疲惫地回了家。"},"sense":{"tw":[["sensible",4],["sensitive",4],["sensor",4],["sensation",4],["feel",0],["smell",0],["detect",2],["understand",2],["logic",3]],"en":"There is a strange sensation in my left hand. I can feel the heat but I cannot feel the cold, and the doctor says the sensor in the skin has stopped working. It is still very sensitive to a light touch. I cannot smell the coffee any more either. The machine can detect the change, but nobody can understand it yet, and there is no logic in it. The doctors say the sense will come back slowly. A sensible person would rest at home, but I have work to do and my hands are the only tools I own.","zh":"我左手有一种奇怪的感觉。我能感觉到热，却感觉不到冷，医生说皮肤里的传感器已经不工作了。但它对轻微的触碰仍然很敏感。我也闻不到咖啡味了。仪器能检测到这个变化，却没人能解释，其中毫无逻辑可言。医生说这种感觉会慢慢恢复。明智的人会在家休息，可我还有活要干，而这双手是我唯一的工具。"},"enter":{"tw":[["entrance",4],["entry",4],["board",3],["exit",1],["record",0],["book",3],["figure",0],["leave",6]],"en":"You cannot enter the old hall through the front entrance any more. The entry in the book says the door was closed in 1974. If you want to go in, board the small bus at the gate and get off at the north exit; the guard will record your name in a thin notebook. I do not know the exact figure of visitors each year, but we never leave the place before six. The key is kept in a shop across the street, and the woman there will only give it to people she already knows.","zh":"你不能再从正门进入那座旧礼堂了。簿子上的记录说那扇门 1974 年就封了。想进去的话，在大门口坐上小巴，从北门下车，守卫会把你的名字记在一个薄本子里。我不知道每年访客的确切数字，但我们从不早于六点离开。钥匙存在街对面的一家店里，那位女士只把钥匙交给她认识的人。"},"form":{"tw":[["formation",4],["formative",4],["build",0],["class",0],["course",0],["body",2],["change",2]],"en":"The formation of a good habit takes months. My formative years were spent in a small school where the class was tiny and the course was fixed for the whole year. We had to build a routine and keep the body moving every morning before the bell. One small change in the order of things, and the whole form of the day falls apart. One winter our teacher was ill for a week, and everything we had built came apart in three days.","zh":"养成一个好习惯要花几个月。我的成长岁月是在一所小学校度过的，那里班级很小，课程整年都固定不变。我们得建立起一套作息，每天早晨铃响前让身体活动起来。只要顺序上有一点小改动，一整天的形态就散了。有一年冬天老师病了一周，我们建起来的那套东西三天就垮了。"},"head":{"tw":[["heady",4],["header",4],["lead",0],["mind",0],["control",2],["chair",3],["foot",1],["chief",6]],"en":"After two cups of that strong wine I felt heady and could hardly stand. My head was hot and my mind was not clear at all. Our chief engineer took control of the meeting, and the chair of the board sat at the end of the long table and did not lead the talk at all. A small header on the first page said 'Do not open'. From head to foot I felt the same strange heat, but nobody at the table seemed to notice; they drank water and went on working.","zh":"喝了两杯那种烈酒之后我觉得头晕，几乎站不住。我的头很热，脑子一点也不清楚。我们的总工程师掌控了会议，而董事会主席坐在长桌尽头，完全没有主导讨论。第一页上有一行小标题写着「请勿打开」。从头到脚我都感到同样奇怪的热，可桌上似乎没人察觉，他们喝着水继续干活。"},"heart":{"tw":[["hearty",4],["cardiac",4],["centre",0],["middle",0],["seat",3],["pain",6],["eye",0],["brain",6]],"en":"My grandfather had a cardiac problem last year. The doctor put a small machine in the centre of his chest, right in the middle, next to the heart. He still gets a pain in the left arm sometimes, but he eats a hearty breakfast and laughs a lot. His brain and his eye are fine, he says; it is only the seat of the trouble that is old. Every afternoon he walks to the end of the street and back, and the machine in his chest keeps the time for him.","zh":"我祖父去年心脏出了毛病。医生在他胸口正中央、紧贴心脏的位置放了一个小装置。他左臂有时还会痛，但他早餐吃得很香，也常笑。他说自己的脑子和眼睛都没问题，年久失修的只是毛病所在的那一处。每天下午他都走到街尾再折回来，胸里那个装置替他计着时间。"},"heat":{"tw":[["geothermal",4],["thermal",4],["cool",1],["cold",6],["temperature",6],["fry",3],["soak",3],["passion",0]],"en":"The geothermal water under this town is very hot. In winter we use it for the thermal baths, and the temperature stays near forty degrees all year. I like to soak in it for an hour, then run outside into the cold air to cool down. My friend cooks an egg in the steam and tries to fry bread on a flat stone. He has a passion for that sort of thing, and the heat never bothers him. In summer the same pipes carry cold water to every house on the street.","zh":"这个小镇地下的地热水很烫。冬天我们用地热浴室，水温全年保持在四十度左右。我喜欢在里面泡上一个小时，再跑到外面的冷空气里降温。我朋友在蒸汽里煮鸡蛋，还试着在一块平石上煎面包。他对这类事情极有热情，再热也从不介意。到了夏天，同一批管子给街上每户人家送冷水。"},"lay":{"tw":[["layer",4],["position",0],["pose",0],["load",3],["organize",2],["bare",6],["move",2],["hand",6]],"en":"We had to lay the old floor again. First we took off the top layer and put every board in the same position on the grass. The workers organize the load into two piles, and I help to hand them the nails. Do not move the wet ones, they say, they will crack in the sun. When the floor is bare, my sister likes to pose for a photograph there. I lay my hand on the cold stone underneath and rest, because the stone is older than the house itself.","zh":"我们得把旧地板重新铺一遍。先揭掉最上面一层，把每块木板按原样摆在草地上。工人们把货分成两堆，我帮忙递钉子。他们说湿的那些别动，太阳一晒会裂。地板露出来以后，我妹妹喜欢在那儿摆姿势拍照。我把手放在底下冰冷的石头上歇一会儿，因为那石头比房子本身还老。"},"line":{"tw":[["lining",4],["liner",4],["air",0],["blood",0],["business",0],["cover",2],["fill",2],["face",3]],"en":"There is a long line at the door of the shop every morning. The lining of my coat is torn, so I wear the old wool liner under it. People in the line talk about the air, about their blood pressure, about business. When the shop opens we fill the small room and cover the counter with our bags. I never see the same face twice. By nine the bread is always gone and the line simply disappears, as if it had never been there.","zh":"每天早上那家店门口都排着长队。我外套的衬里破了，所以里面套着一件旧羊毛内衬。排队的人聊空气、聊血压、聊生意。店门一开，我们就挤满那间小屋，把包堆在柜台上。我从来没见过重复的脸。到九点面包必定卖完，队伍就那样消失了，仿佛从没出现过。"},"picture":{"tw":[["depict",4],["pictorial",4],["photograph",0],["image",2],["illustrate",3],["figure",0],["film",0],["screen",6]],"en":"The picture on my wall is a photograph of the old harbour. It does not depict the whole town, only a small image of the boats. The book next to it is pictorial: every page has a drawing to illustrate one word. I like the figure of the boy in the corner best. In the film they showed last week, the same picture filled the whole screen for a few seconds. I bought it for almost nothing on a wet morning, and I have never wanted to sell it.","zh":"我墙上那幅画是一张旧港的照片。它没有描绘整个镇子，只有小船的一个小影像。旁边那本书是图解式的：每一页都有一幅画来解释一个词。我最喜欢角落里那个男孩的形象。在他们上周放的那部电影里，同一幅画面有几秒钟铺满了整个银幕。我是在一个雨天早晨几乎白捡来的，也从来没想卖掉它。"},"sight":{"tw":[["optic",4],["visual",4],["spectacle",3],["look",2],["position",2],["deal",0],["flood",3]],"en":"The sight from the top of the hill is famous. An optic company put a telescope there, and from that position you can see a visual trick: the sun seems to rise twice. A flood of light hits the valley below, and every look through the glass costs one coin. The whole spectacle lasts two minutes. People come from the next town to see it, and they never say a word while they wait. It is still a good deal for the money.","zh":"山顶上的景致很有名。一家光学公司在那里放了一台望远镜，从那个位置你能看到一个视觉上的把戏：太阳像是升起了两次。一大片光倾泻到下面的山谷，每看一次收一枚硬币。整个奇观持续两分钟。人们从邻镇赶来看，等待时一句话也不说。就这个价钱来说，仍然很划算。"},"sign":{"tw":[["signature",4],["signify",4],["mark",0],["flag",3],["write",2],["contract",0],["alarm",3],["house",0]],"en":"There was no sign on the door of the old house. The only mark I could find was a small flag on the gate and a name that somebody had been asked to write in pencil. The contract in my bag had a signature at the bottom, but I did not know what it was meant to signify. At six the alarm went off and we had to leave the room. Nobody came to explain, and the flag stayed on the gate for another twenty years.","zh":"那座老房子的门上没有任何标志。我能找到的唯一记号是大门上的一面小旗，还有一个被人用铅笔写下的名字。我包里那份合同底部有个签名，但我不知道它意味着什么。六点钟警报响了，我们只好离开那个房间。没人来解释，那面小旗又在门上挂了二十年。"},"stand":{"tw":[["standard",4],["stance",4],["base",0],["bear",0],["continue",2],["fight",2],["lie",1],["hold",6]],"en":"I cannot stand his stance on this question. The standard answer is to wait, but he wants to fight at once. His base is weak: he cannot bear the cost, and if he continues like this the whole plan will not hold. Everything he says seems to lie on one thin idea, and that idea is wrong. Two of his oldest friends left the room before he finished speaking. I stayed, because somebody has to tell him the truth. He will not thank me for it, but a friend who says nothing at all is not a friend.","zh":"我受不了他在这个问题上的立场。标准答案是等等看，可他想立刻开战。他的根基很弱：他承担不起这笔费用，再这样下去整个方案都撑不住。他说的每句话似乎都建立在一条单薄的想法上，而那条想法是错的。他还没说完，两个老朋友就离开了房间。我留了下来，因为总得有人告诉他真相。"},"star":{"tw":[["interstellar",4],["stellar",4],["sun",3],["ace",0],["champion",0],["idol",3],["character",2],["lead",0]],"en":"The star of our team is a quiet boy who never talks about his interstellar dreams. In the stellar light of the evening he runs faster than anyone else, and in the morning sun he trains alone before school begins. He is the ace of the school, our champion for three years, and the idol of every small child here. But his character is what I like most: he does not lead by shouting, and he never laughs at the slower boys.","zh":"我们队的明星是个安静的男孩，从不谈起自己星际旅行的梦想。傍晚的星光下他跑得比谁都快，清晨的太阳里他在开学前独自训练。他是学校的王牌、连续三年的冠军，也是这里每个小孩的偶像。但我最喜欢的是他的品性：他从不靠喊叫来带队，也从不嘲笑跑得慢的孩子。"},"tell":{"tw":[["tale",4],["teller",4],["say",0],["state",0],["express",2],["answer",3],["order",0],["know",6]],"en":"Let me tell you a short tale about a bank teller. He did not say much: he would state the amount, express nothing at all, and answer only yes or no. In order to understand the man you had to know his face. People tell me he was happy in that small room behind the thick glass. He never asked about my money and he never told me his name, but for ten years we said good morning to each other every day.","zh":"让我给你讲一个关于银行出纳员的短故事。他话不多：只报出金额，不流露任何情绪，回答也无非是或否。要理解这个人，你得熟悉他的表情。人们告诉我，他在那层厚玻璃后面的小屋里其实挺快乐。他从不打听我的钱，也从不告诉我他的名字，但十年来我们每天都互道早安。"},"trust":{"tw":[["trustee",4],["fiduciary",4],["believe",2],["hope",0],["credit",3],["count",3],["expect",2],["fund",6]],"en":"You cannot trust a trustee who never writes back. I still believe in him, and I hope he will return, but I do not expect it any more. The fund is small now, and the credit of the office is gone. You can count the people who still trust him on one hand; his fiduciary duty means nothing to the rest of us. His letters are still in my drawer, unopened, and I think they will stay there for a long time.","zh":"你没法信任一个从不回信的受托人。我仍然相信他，也希望他会回来，但我已经不抱期望了。基金现在很少，那间办公室的信誉也没了。还信任他的人一只手就数得过来；他的受托责任对其余的人来说毫无意义。他的信还放在我抽屉里，没有拆开，我想它们会在那里放很久。"},"wave":{"tw":[["waver",4],["wavy",4],["curl",0],["roll",0],["flap",3],["wake",3],["lift",3],["move",2]],"en":"A big wave hit the side of the boat. The wavy line of the water rose, curled and rolled over the deck. The sail began to flap and the wake behind us turned white. I did not move and I did not waver; the lift of the boat felt like a hand under my feet. An hour earlier the sea had been calm as a table, and by night it will be calm again. Only the rope in my hand says that any of this happened.","zh":"一个大浪打在船舷上。起伏的水线升起来，卷曲着翻过甲板。帆开始拍打，我们身后的尾迹变成了白色。我没有动，也没有动摇；船被托起来的感觉就像脚下有一只手。一小时前海面平得像桌面，到了夜里它又会平下来。只有手里这根绳子说明刚才的一切真的发生过。"},"word":{"tw":[["lexical",4],["verbal",4],["phrase",0],["book",0],["news",0],["express",2],["read",6],["order",2]],"en":"One word can change a whole page. I keep a lexical notebook: every verbal form and every short phrase goes into it. When I read the news I copy the words I do not know, in order of how often they appear. A book of ten thousand words is enough to express almost everything, my teacher says, and one wrong word can cost you a friend. I have filled four notebooks since I started, and the fifth is already half full with words I use every day.","zh":"一个词就能改变整页的意思。我有一本词汇笔记本：每个动词形式和每个短语都记进去。看新闻时我把不认识的词抄下来，按出现频率排序。我老师说，一本一万词的书足以表达几乎所有东西，而一个用错的词能让你失去一个朋友。开始记以来我已经写满四个本子。"},"death":{"tw":[["die",4],["dead",6],["mortuary",4],["end",2],["grave",3],["birth",1],["destruction",0],["demise",0]],"en":"The death of the old king changed everything. Few people died in the war itself, but the destruction of the city killed the trade. In the mortuary they counted the bodies, and the dead were carried out at dawn. The grave of his father stood next to the new one. His birth had been a feast; his demise was a silence, and the end came quietly. For a whole year afterwards the shops stayed shut and nobody sang in the streets.","zh":"老国王的死改变了一切。战争本身没死几个人，但城市的毁灭扼杀了贸易。在停尸房里他们清点遗体，死者于黎明时被抬走。他父亲的墓就在新墓旁边。他的出生曾是一场盛宴，他的离世却是一片寂静，结局来得悄无声息。此后整整一年，店铺都关着，街上再没人唱歌。"},"nose":{"tw":[["nosy",4],["nasal",4],["snout",3],["scent",0],["poke",0],["push",2],["throat",6],["front",2]],"en":"The dog has a cold nose and a very nasal bark. Its snout is always in the long grass, following some scent. Do not poke it and do not push it away; it will only come back. The hair on its throat is white, and the front of its face is black. My nosy neighbour says the dog knows everything that happens in this street. During the heat of the day it sleeps under the table and does not move at all.","zh":"那只狗鼻子凉凉的，叫声带着很重的鼻音。它的口鼻总埋在深草里，追着某种气味。别去戳它，也别把它推开，它只会再回来。它喉咙上的毛是白的，脸的前部是黑的。我那位爱打听的邻居说，这条街上发生的事这只狗全知道。白天最热的时候它就趴在桌子底下睡，一动也不动。"},"office":{"tw":[["official",4],["officiate",4],["position",0],["post",0],["headquarters",3],["duty",2],["staff",2],["department",6]],"en":"The office is on the third floor of an old building. The official letter says my position starts on Monday. Our headquarters is in another city, and this post is only a small department of four people. The staff are kind. My first duty is to answer the phone; I also have to officiate at the morning meeting. The lift has not worked since March, so we all take the stairs, and the stairs are the only place where anybody speaks freely.","zh":"办公室在一栋旧楼的三层。公函上说我的职位周一开始。我们的总部在另一个城市，这个岗位只是一个四人的小部门。同事们都很和气。我的第一项职责是接电话，还得主持晨会。电梯从三月起就坏了，所以我们全都走楼梯，而楼梯是唯一能让人畅所欲言的地方。"},"please":{"tw":[["pleasant",4],["pleasure",4],["delight",0],["satisfy",2],["enchant",3],["wish",2],["displease",1],["ask",6]],"en":"It is hard to please my aunt. A pleasant word in the morning will delight her, but nothing can satisfy her for long. The garden does not enchant her any more. I only wish she would ask for what she wants; then I could please her at once. Last week I displeased her by arriving late. It is no pleasure to sit in that room with her. She says the house is too quiet, and I think that is the whole trouble.","zh":"要让我姑妈满意很难。早上一句好听的话能让她高兴，但什么都不能让她满意太久。花园已经不再让她着迷了。我只希望她能把想要的东西说出来，那样我马上就能让她高兴。上周我迟到惹她不快。和她坐在那个房间里毫无乐趣可言。她说屋子太安静了，我想这就是全部的问题所在。"},"water":{"tw":[["aquatic",4],["hydraulic",4],["irrigate",0],["wet",2],["dry",6],["fill",2],["sand",6]],"en":"The water in this valley comes from a spring. In summer we irrigate the fields with it, and the hydraulic pump is old but still works. The aquatic plants near the edge stay wet all year, while the sand on the far side is dry. Every evening I fill two bottles and carry them home. In winter the spring slows down and we have to walk much further for the same two bottles. My mother says the spring has never once failed us, and I hope that is still true.","zh":"这个山谷里的水来自一眼泉。夏天我们用它灌溉田地，那台水泵很旧但还能用。靠边的水生植物终年是湿的，而远处那片沙子却是干的。每天傍晚我灌满两瓶水带回家。到了冬天泉水流得慢，为同样两瓶水我们得走远得多的路。"},"admit":{"tw":[["admission",4],["accept",2],["allow",0],["permit",2],["deny",1],["acknowledge",6],["seat",3],["serve",2]],"en":"They will not admit more than fifty people. The admission desk is at the door: if they accept your ticket they allow you in, but the permit is only for one hour. They deny nothing and acknowledge every question, yet the room can serve only a few at a time. I could not find a single empty seat. Outside, a hundred people were still waiting in the rain, and nobody there looked angry. They simply waited while the rain fell on their coats and on the stone steps of the hall.","zh":"他们最多只放进五十个人。售票处在门口：如果他们收下你的票就允许你进去，但许可只限一小时。他们什么也不否认，对每个问题都有回应，可那间屋子一次只能招待几个人。我一个空座位都没找到。外面还有一百个人在雨里等着，而那边没有一个人显得生气。"},"arm":{"tw":[["armament",4],["disarm",1],["weapon",0],["sword",3],["bow",3],["instrument",2],["limb",2],["finger",6]],"en":"He hurt his left arm in the factory last month. The limb was not broken, but he cannot lift a heavy instrument any more, and his fingers are slow in the cold. In the old armament room next door they keep weapons behind glass: a bow, a sword, two long guns. The guard had to disarm a man there once, and the story is still told in the village. My brother works with one hand now and laughs about it. He says a man only needs one good arm to do the work of two.","zh":"他上个月在工厂里伤了左臂。那条胳膊没断，但他再也不能举起重工具了，天冷时手指也不灵活。隔壁那间旧军械室里，武器都用玻璃罩着：一张弓、一把剑、两杆长枪。守卫曾在那里缴过一个人的械，这事村里至今还在讲。我哥哥现在只用一只手干活，还拿这事开玩笑。他说一个人只要有一条好胳膊，就能干两条胳膊的活。"},"better":{"tw":[["bet",4],["best",0],["improve",0],["worse",1],["change",2],["build",3],["break",0],["help",3]],"en":"I made a bet with myself last spring. The best way to get better at this job, I decided, is to build one small habit and never break it. A change of hours will help; working later only makes things worse. I want to improve slowly, not quickly. My brother says I should rest more, and I am sure he is right, because he is a good worker and I am not. So far I have kept the bet for eleven weeks, and the work is easier than it was.","zh":"去年春天我和自己打了个赌。我认定，要把这活儿做得更好，最好的办法是养成一个小习惯并且不打破它。改一改作息会有帮助；干到更晚只会让情况更糟。我要慢慢提高，而不是求快。我哥哥说我该多休息，我确信他是对的，因为他是个好工人而我不是。到现在这个赌我守了十一周，活儿也比从前轻松了。"},"home":{"tw":[["homely",4],["homestead",3],["house",2],["family",0],["return",2],["away",1],["lodge",3],["rest",6],["environment",2]],"en":"My idea of home is a homely room with one window. The house is small, but the homestead behind it has been in our family for four generations. When I return from the city I sleep for twelve hours; away from it I cannot rest at all. My friends lodge in a hotel two streets from here and say the environment is the same anywhere. I tell them they are wrong, and that one room you know is worth more than a big one you do not.","zh":"我心目中的家是一个带一扇窗的朴素房间。房子很小，可屋后那片宅地已属于我们家四代人了。从城里回来时我能睡上十二个小时；离开它我就完全无法休息。我的朋友们住在两条街外的一家旅馆，说环境在哪里都一样。我告诉他们他们错了，一间你熟悉的屋子比一间你不熟悉的大屋子值钱得多。"},"let":{"tw":[["letter",4],["allow",3],["accept",2],["prevent",1],["rent",0],["lease",0],["admit",3],["leave",2]],"en":"They will not let us sign the lease before June. The letter says the owner will allow three people in the flat, but he will not accept a dog. Nothing can prevent him from changing his mind either, and he will not admit that the price is too high. We rent the top floor now and pay by the week. If he decides to leave the country, we will have to find another place before the summer ends. The dog sleeps under the table in the kitchen and has never once barked at anybody.","zh":"他们不允许我们在六月前签租约。信上说房东允许三个人住这套公寓，但不接受养狗。也没什么能阻止他改主意，而他也不肯承认价格太高。我们现在租顶层，按周付钱。如果他决定出国，我们就得在夏天结束前另找住处。"},"light":{"tw":[["lightly",4],["clean",0],["clear",0],["flood",3],["surface",6],["dark",1],["burn",2],["match",3],["easy",5]],"en":"The light in this room is strange. It is clean and clear in the morning, when a flood of sun hits the white surface of the wall, but by four o'clock it is almost dark. I burn one candle and read by it, or I strike a match and walk to the window. Sleep comes lightly here; the dark does not feel heavy and the light does not hurt my eyes. It is easy to work in this room, and just as easy to stop working.","zh":"这屋子里的光很奇怪。清晨它干净而清澈，一大片阳光打在墙的白色表面上，可到四点就几乎黑了。我点一支蜡烛就着光读书，或者划根火柴走到窗前。在这里睡觉很浅；黑暗并不沉重，光也不刺眼。在这屋里很容易干活，也同样很容易就停下不干。"},"mind":{"tw":[["mental",4],["head",0],["tend",3],["forget",1],["manage",2],["worry",3],["notice",2],["idea",0],["listen",0]],"en":"There is too much in my mind this week. My head is full of small numbers, and I tend to forget names. The doctor says it is not a mental problem, only tiredness. I try to manage one thing at a time. Do not worry, she says, and notice what you eat. It is a good idea, and I should listen to her, but I never do. My mother had the same mind and the same habit of not listening to anybody.","zh":"这星期我脑子里装的东西太多了。我满脑子都是小数字，还容易忘名字。医生说这不是精神上的问题，只是累。我试着一次只处理一件事。别担心，她说，注意你吃的东西。这是个好主意，我该听她的，可我从来不听。我母亲也有同样的脑子，也有同样的、谁的话都不听的习惯。"},"notice":{"tw":[["notify",4],["bill",0],["knock",3],["sign",2],["ignore",1],["check",6],["card",0],["discover",0],["mention",3]],"en":"Did you notice the notice on the door? A small card says we must notify the office if we leave. Nobody told me about it; they did not even knock. There is a sign above the bell, but people ignore it every single day. I had to check the bill three times before I discovered the extra line at the bottom. When I asked about it, the man at the desk did not mention it once. He only looked at his hands.","zh":"你注意到门上那张告示了吗？一张小卡片说我们离开时必须通知办公室。没人跟我说过这件事，他们连门都没敲。铃上方有个标牌，可人们每天都视而不见。我把账单核对了三遍，才发现底部多出的那一行。我去问时，柜台后面那个人一次也没提。他只是看着自己的手。"},"pass":{"tw":[["passage",4],["clear",3],["break",3],["change",2],["fail",1],["carry",3],["leave",2],["draw",0]],"en":"You cannot pass this road in winter. The passage over the hill is clear for only three months, and one bad storm can break it completely. If the weather does not change, we will fail to reach the village at all. Two men carry the mail on foot and leave before dawn. I draw a map every year and it is never the same twice. Still, the post always gets through in the end, and that is the only thing that matters up here.","zh":"冬天你没法通过这条路。翻过山口那条通道只有三个月是通的，一场坏风暴就能把它彻底毁掉。如果天气不变，我们根本到不了那个村子。两个人徒步送信，天不亮就出发。我每年画一张地图，从来没重过样。可邮件最后总能送到，而在这山里那是唯一要紧的事。"},"present":{"tw":[["presence",4],["face",0],["date",3],["inform",2],["past",1],["stage",0],["state",2],["deliver",0]],"en":"At present there is no water in the tank. The presence of two engineers did not help; they only informed us of the date of the repair and left. On the stage above the door someone has written the state of the pump every day for ten years. In the past we never had to check it. The man who comes to deliver the parts knows the problem by heart, but he did not show his face for three days.","zh":"目前水箱里没有水。两位工程师在场也没用；他们只是通知了我们维修的日期就走了。门上方那块平台上，有人十年来每天都记下水泵的状态。从前我们根本不用检查。来送零件的那个人对这个问题了如指掌，可他整整三天没露面。"},"sound":{"tw":[["soundly",4],["voice",0],["acoustic",6],["noise",3],["silence",1],["heavy",0],["blow",3],["announce",2],["good",5]],"en":"The sound in the old hall is beautiful. A single voice fills it, and the acoustic roof holds every note. There is no noise from the street, only a heavy silence between the songs. When the singer stops you can hear the wind blow across the roof. The man at the door will announce the next piece in a low voice. At night the whole building sleeps soundly. It is a good place to sit and think, and nobody asks you to leave.","zh":"那座旧厅里的声音很美。一个人的嗓音就能填满它，声学屋顶留住了每一个音。街上没有噪音，歌声之间只有沉沉的寂静。歌手停下时，你能听见风掠过屋顶。门口那个人会用低沉的嗓音报出下一曲。夜里整栋楼睡得很沉。那是个适合坐着想事的好地方，也没人赶你走。"},"base":{"tw":[["basal",4],["bag",0],["bed",3],["bottom",2],["floor",0],["build",3],["control",2],["foot",0]],"en":"The base of the old tower is wider than the top. At the bottom there is a thick basal layer of stone, and below that only sand. We had to build a floor of wood over it so that nobody would fall through. Every bag of tools sits in the corner. From the control room you can see the whole valley, and it is a long way down to the foot of the hill. A bed of dry grass used to cover the stone, but the rain took it years ago.","zh":"那座古塔的基部比顶部宽。底部有一层很厚的基底石，再往下就只有沙子了。我们不得不在上面铺一层木地板，免得有人掉下去。每袋工具都堆在角落里。从控制室能看到整个山谷，往下到山脚还有很长一段路。从前有一层干草铺在石头上，但多年前就被雨水冲走了。"},"bet":{"tw":[["count",0],["pot",3],["trust",2],["raise",3],["gamble",2],["cash",6],["play",3],["better",4]],"en":"Do not bet on that horse. I do not trust the man who owns it, and I can count the times he has actually paid on one hand. The pot is small tonight, but he will raise it as soon as you sit down. My cousin likes to gamble and always plays with cash. You will feel better if you keep your money in your pocket. I learned that lesson in a single evening, and it was not a cheap one to learn.","zh":"别赌那匹马。我不信任它的主人，他真正付过钱的次数我一只手就数得过来。今晚的赌池很小，可你一坐下他就会加注。我表弟喜欢赌，而且总是用现金玩。把钱留在口袋里你会好受些。我是在一个晚上学会这个教训的，而那学费并不便宜。"},"board":{"tw":[["boarder",4],["card",0],["catch",3],["enter",2],["commission",6],["room",0],["deal",3],["table",2]],"en":"The board meets at eight. Each member puts a card on the table, and the chairman reads out the name of every boarder in the house. We deal with one question at a time, and only one. A small commission was set up last year to check the accounts, and nobody has entered that room since March. I try to catch the chairman before the meeting, but he is never alone. Last week they sat for four hours and decided nothing at all.","zh":"董事会八点开会。每位成员把一张卡片放在桌上，主席逐一念出屋里每位寄宿者的名字。我们一次只处理一个问题，而且只处理一个。去年成立了一个小委员会来查账，可自三月起没人进过那个房间。我想在会前逮住主席，可他从没落单过。上周他们坐了四个小时，什么也没定下来。"},"carry":{"tw":[["carriage",4],["bear",2],["deal",3],["act",2],["express",0],["fly",3],["bring",2],["hold",0]],"en":"I have to carry these boxes to the station. The carriage of the train leaves in an hour, and the porter will not bear more than two at a time. We deal with the heaviest first and then act quickly. If we are late they will not hold the train, and my sister will have to bring the rest tomorrow. The express never stops here. Nothing flies out of this town, so everything goes by rail. The porter says the same thing every winter, and every winter he turns out to be right.","zh":"我得把这些箱子搬到车站去。那趟火车的车厢一小时后开，搬运工一次不肯扛超过两箱。我们先处理最重的，然后动作要快。要是迟了他们不会等车，剩下的就得让我妹妹明天带来。快车从不停这里。这个镇上什么也飞不出去，所以一切都走铁路。"},"catch":{"tw":[["catchment",4],["see",0],["bag",3],["board",2],["stop",0],["fish",3],["throw",6],["view",0]],"en":"We could not catch a single fish all morning. The catchment above the dam is full of rain water and the fish are deep. I stood on the board and could not see a thing; my bag was still empty at noon. Then one careless throw of a stone by a boy on the far bank moved the whole shoal at once. From where I stood the view was lovely, but that does not stop me from wanting one fish. Next week I will try the other side, where the water is slower.","zh":"整个上午我们一条鱼也没抓到。水坝上游的集水区灌满了雨水，鱼都沉在深处。我站在木板上什么也看不见；到了中午我的袋子还是空的。后来一个男孩扔了块石头，整群鱼一下子全动了。从我站的地方看出去景色很美，可这并不能阻止我想要一条鱼。下周我要去另一边试试，那边水流更缓。"},"count":{"tw":[["counter",4],["bet",0],["total",3],["depend",0],["poll",3],["trust",2],["result",6],["look",0]],"en":"We count the votes twice. The counter at the front of the room is an old wooden table, and the total is written on the wall in chalk. You cannot depend on one count, and you cannot trust the first result either. At the last poll two hundred people came, and the look on his face said everything. I would bet the second count is the true one. Nobody argues after the second count; they simply pick up their coats and go home.","zh":"我们把票点两遍。屋子前面那张计数器是一张旧木桌，总数用粉笔写在墙上。你不能只靠一次计数，也不能相信第一次的结果。上一次投票来了两百人，而他脸上的表情说明了一切。我敢打赌第二次计数才是真的。第二次计数之后没人再争，他们只是拿起外套回家。"},"die":{"tw":[["death",4],["break",0],["fall",3],["change",2],["pass",0],["crash",3],["feel",2],["fail",0]],"en":"Old engines do not die all at once. First a small part breaks, then the pressure falls, and the change is very slow. You can feel it in the steering wheel months before the end. If the pump fails, the car will crash into the wall at the next bend. The death of an engine is a long story, and most of it happens quietly. Mine passed away on a Tuesday, in front of my own house, with the key still in the door.","zh":"老发动机不会一下子死掉。先是某个小零件坏掉，接着压力下降，变化非常慢。在结局到来前几个月，你就能在方向盘上感觉到。如果水泵失灵，车会在下一个弯道撞上墙。一台发动机的死亡是个漫长的故事，而且大部分是悄无声息地发生的。我那台是在一个星期二咽气的，就在我自己家门口，钥匙还插在门上。"},"doctor":{"tw":[["doctoral",4],["fix",0],["fill",3],["better",2],["nurse",6],["repair",0],["piece",3],["restore",0]],"en":"The doctor came at seven. He fixed my arm, filled a small cup with something bitter, and said I would feel better in a week. A nurse held the lamp; she said the same doctor had repaired her father's leg and restored it to full use. He showed me one small piece of bone in the palm of his hand. He is writing a doctoral paper about exactly this sort of injury. He told me I was lucky, and I did not argue with him.","zh":"医生七点来的。他给我接好了胳膊，倒了一小杯很苦的东西，说我一周后就会好些。一位护士举着灯；她说同一位医生修好过她父亲的腿，并让它完全恢复了功能。他摊开手掌给我看一小块骨头。他正在写一篇关于这类损伤的博士论文。他说我很幸运，我没有跟他争。"},"draw":{"tw":[["drawer",4],["force",0],["arrange",2],["match",6],["line",0],["catch",3],["win",6],["lot",0]],"en":"Let us draw for the first turn. In the drawer of the little table there are four cards; arrange them face down and each of us takes one. Catch your card before it falls on the floor. The match is won by the highest line, so look at it carefully. I never win anything by luck, and a lot of people at this table say the same. You can force the card if you want, but then there is no point in playing at all.","zh":"咱们抽签决定先手吧。小桌的抽屉里有四张牌；把它们正面朝下摆好，每人拿一张。牌掉到地上之前接住它。比赛由点数最大的那一行获胜，所以要看仔细。我从来没靠运气赢过什么，这张桌上很多人也这么说。你想的话可以硬来，但那样玩起来就没意思了。"},"drive":{"tw":[["drift",4],["cause",0],["lift",3],["fight",2],["force",0],["pull",3],["hit",2],["push",0]],"en":"It is a long drive to the coast. The road begins to drift west after the bridge, and the wind can cause the car to lift on the open bends. My father would push the speed up and then pull it back again; he never liked to fight the wheel. One year a stone hit the glass and we ran the last ten miles with no window at all. I drive slowly now, and the force of the wind still surprises me every time.","zh":"开车到海边要走很久。过了桥这条路就开始向西偏，在开阔的弯道上风能把车掀起来。我父亲会把速度推上去再收回来；他从不喜欢跟方向盘较劲。有一年一块石头打在玻璃上，我们最后十英里是没窗跑完的。我现在开得慢，而每次那股风力还是让我吃惊。"},"earth":{"tw":[["terrestrial",4],["ground",2],["floor",3],["concern",2],["space",6],["land",0],["forest",3],["hide",2],["world",0]],"en":"The earth here is red and thin. On the ground under the trees there is a soft floor of leaves, and the forest hides more than it shows. Scientists come to study the terrestrial plants; others look up at the space above the trees and forget the land under their feet. Their only concern is the rain, and the rain comes when it wants to. For me this small piece of earth is the whole world, and I do not want to leave it.","zh":"这里的土又红又薄。树下的地面上铺着一层松软的落叶，森林藏起来的比露出来的多。科学家来研究陆生植物；另一些人抬头看树顶以上的太空，却忘了脚下的土地。他们唯一关心的是雨，而雨想来就来。对我来说这一小块土地就是整个世界，我不想离开它。"},"edge":{"tw":[["edgy",4],["inch",0],["shoulder",3],["line",2],["march",0],["margin",3],["side",2],["border",3],["corner",6]],"en":"We walked along the edge of the field for an hour. The border with the next farm is only a line of small stones, and the margin of the wood lies on the far side. At the corner an old man was marching up and down with his shoulder against the wind. I moved an inch at a time, because the drop below was long. My friend felt edgy and would not look down once the whole way. We sat down at last, well back from the edge, and ate the bread we had brought.","zh":"我们沿着田边走了一个小时。与隔壁农场的分界只是一排小石头，树林的边缘在更远的一侧。拐角处有个老人顶着风来回踱步，肩膀迎着风口。我一次只挪一寸，因为下面的落差很大。我朋友一路上都很紧张，一次也没敢往下看。"},"face":{"tw":[["facial",4],["front",2],["bottom",3],["cover",2],["look",0],["top",3],["lie",2],["present",0]],"en":"I did not want to face him again. His face was in the front room, at the top of the stairs, and the look on it had not changed at all. He would not lie down and sat in the chair by the window all night. The bottom of the door was covered with old letters that nobody had opened. His facial expression was calm, too calm. At present I still do not know what I said to him that evening.","zh":"我不想再面对他。他的脸在前面那间屋里、楼梯顶端，脸上的表情一点没变。他不肯躺下，整夜坐在窗边那把椅子上。门的下半部堆满了没人拆过的旧信。他的面部表情很平静，平静得过分。直到现在我也不知道那天晚上我对他说了什么。"},"fire":{"tw":[["fiery",4],["burn",0],["bake",2],["hire",1],["raise",0],["excite",3],["explosion",6],["attack",2]],"en":"The fire started in the bakery at two. The old oven was still burning when we came, and the smell of baked bread was everywhere in the street. Someone raised the alarm, and the explosion of the gas bottle woke the whole neighbourhood. It was a fiery hour, and the thought of it still excites me. Nobody knows what could attack the wiring like that. They will not hire a new baker until the roof is fixed. The cat was found two streets away the next morning, asleep under a car.","zh":"火灾是两点在面包房起的。我们赶到时那个旧烤炉还在烧，街上到处是烤面包的味道。有人拉响了警报，煤气瓶的爆炸惊醒了整个街区。那是火光冲天的一小时，现在想起来还让我激动。没人知道是什么能那样侵蚀线路。屋顶修好之前他们不会雇新面包师。"},"fix":{"tw":[["fixture",4],["cook",0],["care",3],["better",2],["plug",6],["doctor",0],["dress",3],["hole",0]],"en":"Can you fix this lamp? The fixture is loose and the plug is broken. My brother cooked dinner while I worked, and my sister dressed the children and put them to bed. There is a hole in the wall behind the lamp that I cannot fill. The doctor who lived here before us took better care of this house than we ever did. I will fix it properly on Sunday. Until then we will sit in the dark and talk, which is not such a bad thing.","zh":"你能修一下这盏灯吗？灯具松了，插头也坏了。我干活时我哥哥做了晚饭，我姐姐给孩子们穿好衣服哄他们上床。灯后面墙上有个洞，我填不上。住在我们之前的那位医生对这房子比我们上心得多。我周日会好好修它。在那之前我们就摸黑坐着说话，这也算不上什么坏事。"},"green":{"tw":[["greenery",4],["park",0],["sprout",3],["site",2],["ripe",1],["emerald",3],["vegetable",2]],"en":"The green field behind the house turns yellow in July. The greenery along the river is thick, and in spring every small sprout comes up between the stones. We chose the site for the new park because it stays green all year. The emerald water below the bridge is cold, and the vegetable garden next to it is not ripe yet. My mother says green is the only colour she can trust. She has planted the same three rows for forty years.","zh":"屋后那片绿色的田到七月就变黄了。河边的草木很茂密，春天每一个小芽都从石缝里钻出来。我们把新公园选在这里，是因为它整年都是绿的。桥下那水呈翡翠色，很凉；旁边的菜园还没熟。我母亲说绿色是她唯一能信任的颜色。同一片三行地她种了四十年。"},"hand":{"tw":[["manual",4],["deal",3],["pass",0],["reach",0],["left",3],["right",3],["side",2],["hard",6]],"en":"Take my hand and do not let go. The manual says you must deal with the switch with your left hand only, and pass nothing to the other side of the machine. If you can reach the lever, pull it once and pull it hard. On the right there is a small wheel, and on the back a box of tools. My grandfather worked with either hand and never read a manual in his life. He says the hand knows more than the head, and for this job he is right.","zh":"抓住我的手，别松开。手册上说，操作这个开关只能用左手，而且不能把任何东西递到机器的另一侧。如果你够得到那根杠杆，就拉一次，用力拉。右边有个小轮子，后面有个工具箱。我祖父两只手都能干活，一辈子没读过手册。他说手比脑子懂得多，干这活儿他说得对。"},"lock":{"tw":[["locker",4],["curl",0],["engage",0],["hold",2],["hook",6],["mesh",0],["hair",2],["prop",6]],"en":"The lock on the old locker is broken. Inside there is a rope, a metal hook and a piece of mesh that used to hold the window shut. You have to engage the small lever first, then turn the key twice, and only then will the prop stay in place. My sister's hair was caught in it once, in a single curl, and she has never touched the door since. I keep a spare key in my pocket for the days when it refuses to open.","zh":"那个旧储物柜的锁坏了。里面有一根绳子、一个金属钩子，还有一块以前用来顶住窗户的铁丝网。你得先把小杠杆卡上，然后把钥匙转两圈，这样撑杆才待得住。我姐姐的头发曾被卷进去过一缕，从那以后她再没碰过那扇门。我在口袋里放了一把备用钥匙，专对付它打不开的日子。"},"mouth":{"tw":[["oral",4],["lip",0],["shout",3],["tongue",6],["speak",0],["sing",3],["communicate",2],["talk",0]],"en":"Keep your mouth closed when you chew. The oral exam next week will test how you open a speech, and my teacher wants us to speak slowly. When you shout, the tongue moves differently than when you sing. She says a mouth can talk all day and communicate nothing at all. Her lower lip is dry and her voice is thin now. Do not touch the microphone with your lips. My mother puts a finger to her lips whenever I open mine at the table.","zh":"嚼东西的时候把嘴闭上。下周的口试要考你怎么开头演讲，老师要我们说慢一点。喊的时候，舌头的动作和唱歌时不一样。她说一张嘴能说一整天却什么也没表达。她的下唇很干，嗓音如今也细弱了。别用嘴唇碰麦克风。"},"move":{"tw":[["motion",4],["act",2],["beat",3],["cause",2],["continue",6],["run",0],["begin",3],["change",2]],"en":"We have to move the piano before Friday. The motion of the truck on these roads will damage it, so we wrap every leg in cloth. I cannot act alone; two people have to lift at the same time, to the same beat. Nothing will cause more trouble than the stairs. If it starts to rain we will begin again in the morning. Water can change the shape of wood in one night, so we cannot stay outside. The whole move should take two hours if nobody runs. We will continue with the small boxes indoors.","zh":"我们得在周五前把钢琴搬走。卡车在这些路上的颠簸会把它弄坏，所以我们把每条腿都裹上布。我一个人做不了；两个人得同时抬，按同一个节拍。没有比那几级楼梯更麻烦的了。要是下起雨来，我们就第二天早上重来。水一夜之间就能改变木头的形状，所以不能放在外面。只要没人乱跑，整个搬运两小时就能完。"},"name":{"tw":[["nominal",4],["call",0],["refer",6],["discover",0],["raise",3],["appoint",2],["family",2],["figure",0]],"en":"Nobody knows the real name of the old man at the gate. People call him 'the captain', but that is only a nominal title; nobody has been able to discover where it came from. His family name is carved above the door, and I have to refer to it every morning when I raise the flag. The committee will appoint a new watchman in June. The figure of a woman on the gate carries the same name. Even the map of the town carries the same name in its corner. It has been there since 1893, and nobody has ever tried to change it.","zh":"没人知道大门口那位老人的真名。大家叫他「船长」，可那只是个名义上的称呼；没人能查清它的来历。他的姓氏刻在门楣上，我每天早上升旗时都得提到它。委员会六月要任命一名新看守。大门上那个女人的雕像也带着同一个名字。"},"need":{"tw":[["needy",4],["ask",0],["want",0],["demand",0],["cost",3],["condition",2],["poverty",2],["cry",3]],"en":"Tell me what you need. Do not ask twice and do not demand; just say it once. The cost of the repairs is small, but the condition of the roof is not, and sooner or later we will have to deal with it. There are two needy families in this street, and one of them lives in real poverty. I heard a child cry last night, in the house at the corner. I am sure they want nothing more than a warm room.","zh":"告诉我你需要什么。别问两遍，也别强求，说一次就够了。修理的花费不大，可屋顶的状况不好，迟早得处理。这条街上有两户穷苦人家，其中一户真的是一贫如洗。昨晚我听见一个孩子在哭，就在拐角那栋房子里。我敢肯定，他们想要的不过是一间暖和的屋子。"},"note":{"tw":[["annotate",4],["bill",0],["quote",6],["line",0],["mark",0],["read",6],["state",2],["excuse",3]],"en":"I left a note on the table. It says the bill has been paid and the spare key is under the pot. I had to annotate the last page, because the small line at the bottom is easy to miss. Do not quote me on any of this, and do not read the note to the king; he will only look for an excuse. The state of the accounts is written in the same note, and I put a mark next to every name.","zh":"我在桌上留了张字条。上面写着账单已经付了，备用钥匙在花盆底下。最后一页我不得不加注，因为底下那一小行很容易看漏。这些话别引我的话，也别把字条念给国王听，他只会找个借口。账目状况也写在同一张字条上，我在每个名字旁都做了记号。"},"nurse":{"tw":[["nursery",4],["hold",0],["midwife",3],["care",2],["entertain",0],["matron",3],["feed",2],["nanny",0]],"en":"The nurse comes at six and the matron at eight. In the nursery next door there are twelve small beds, and a nanny feeds the smallest ones by hand. The midwife who delivered my brother still works here; she says care is the only medicine that never runs out. I hold the lamp for her while she works. She will entertain the children for an hour and then send them all to bed. In the winter she stays until midnight, and nobody asks her to. The children call her by her first name, which the matron does not like at all.","zh":"护士六点来，护士长八点来。隔壁的育婴室里摆着十二张小床，一位保姆用手一口口喂最小的那几个。当年接生我弟弟的助产士如今还在这儿干；她说照护是唯一永远不会用完的药。她干活时我替她举着灯。她会陪孩子们玩一个小时，然后把他们全都打发上床。"},"position":{"tw":[["posit",4],["lay",0],["dress",3],["move",2],["office",0],["face",3],["state",2],["post",0]],"en":"My position in the office is a small one. I lay out the letters in the morning and move the files from one post to another. The face of the building is being repaired, so we dress the windows with paper. I would posit that nobody here knows what the final state of the plan will be. However, we will keep working. The sign on the door still carries the old name. Every day I do the same three things, and every day they take the same time. My desk is by the window, and I can see the river from it.","zh":"我在办公室里的职位很小。早上我把信件摊开，把文件从一个岗位挪到另一个岗位。大楼的正面正在维修，所以我们用纸把窗户糊起来。我敢假定这里没人知道这个计划最终的状态是什么。不管怎样，我们还会继续干。门上的牌子还挂着旧名字。"},"post":{"tw":[["poster",4],["carry",0],["express",3],["call",2],["press",6],["office",0],["locate",3],["list",2],["position",0]],"en":"Every post brings two letters and a newspaper. The office cannot locate the missing parcel, and nobody can tell me which list it is on. I put a poster on the wall: 'Do not post cash'. We carry the bags to the express box before nine, and the press calls us every afternoon, sometimes twice. My position here is simple: I sort the mail and I keep quiet. At Christmas the bags are so heavy that two of us have to carry them. Nobody writes letters any more, they say, but the bags are never lighter.","zh":"每一班邮件送来两封信和一份报纸。办公室查不到那个丢失的包裹，也没人告诉我它在哪张清单上。我在墙上贴了张海报：「勿寄现金」。九点前我们把邮袋送到快递箱，报社每天下午都打电话来，有时打两次。我在这里的岗位很简单：分拣邮件，闭嘴干活。"},"race":{"tw":[["run",0],["heat",3],["act",2],["contest",6],["wash",0],["tear",3],["move",2],["rush",0]],"en":"The race begins at noon. Nobody can act as if it is only a game: the heat of the day will decide half of it. We watch from the bank, where the water can wash the mud off our shoes. A hundred people run, and the crowd cannot move at all when the rush starts at the first corner. This contest is older than the town. One year the wind was strong enough to tear every flag off the poles.","zh":"比赛中午开始。谁也不能装作这只是一场游戏：当天的暑气会决定一半的胜负。我们在河岸上看，那里的水能洗掉鞋上的泥。一百个人在跑，第一个弯道拥挤开始时，人群根本动不了。这项比赛比镇子还老。有一年风大得把所有旗子都从杆子上扯了下来。"},"sing":{"tw":[["song",4],["talk",2],["chant",3],["sound",2],["tune",6],["whistle",0],["hum",3],["listen",6],["interpret",2]],"en":"Please sing that song again. My grandmother could talk about music for hours; she said every tune has a sound of its own. In the old church they chant without a book, and the children hum along. When I was small I could only whistle, never sing. I listen to the same three songs every winter, and each time I interpret the words a little differently. The last line is always the same, and that is why I remember it. If you want, we can sing it together on Sunday evening.","zh":"请把那首歌再唱一遍。我祖母谈起音乐能说上几个小时；她说每支曲子都有自己独特的声音。在那座旧教堂里，人们不看谱子吟唱，孩子们跟着哼。我小时候只会吹口哨，从不会唱。每年冬天我都听同样的三首歌，而每一次我对歌词的理解都略有不同。"},"skin":{"tw":[["skinny",4],["bark",0],["scalp",3],["hide",0],["jacket",3],["bag",2],["breast",6],["struggle",0],["climb",2]],"en":"The skin on his hands is hard and dark. He is skinny now, and his jacket hangs loose on him. A leather bag, made from the hide of an old cow, sits on the floor next to his boots. The bark of the tree outside is rough, like his scalp. He has a mark on his breast, near the throat, from a struggle twenty years ago. Every winter he has to climb the same hill twice a day. He says the cold has taken the feeling out of it, and he does not miss it.","zh":"他手上的皮肤又硬又黑。他如今很瘦，夹克挂在身上空荡荡的。一个用老牛皮做的皮包放在地上，挨着他的靴子。外面那棵树的树皮很粗糙，就像他的头皮。他胸口靠近喉咙处有一道疤，是二十年前一场扭打留下的。每年冬天他都得每天爬两次那座山。"},"speak":{"tw":[["speech",4],["address",0],["sound",2],["listen",6],["mouth",0],["shout",3],["communicate",2],["continue",3]],"en":"I cannot speak in front of a crowd. My speech was ready, but when I stood up my mouth went dry and the sound of the room was louder than my voice. People began to shout from the back. I tried to continue and then to address one man only. It is easier to listen than to speak, and much easier to keep quiet. Next time I will try to communicate something shorter. My hands shake when the room is quiet, and they shake even more when it is not.","zh":"我无法在人前讲话。讲稿早就写好了，可我一站起来嘴就发干，屋里的声音比我的嗓音还大。后面的人开始喊。我试着继续说下去，接着只对着一个人讲。听比说容易，闭嘴不说更容易。下次我要试着讲短一点。"},"state":{"tw":[["civil",4],["country",0],["propose",2],["express",2],["answer",3],["attribute",2],["law",6],["land",0],["add",3]],"en":"The state of the roads is the main question here. Our country has a new law about land, and the administration wants to add three more. I cannot propose anything better: no state can express what the farmers feel when the water comes. You can attribute the damage to the rain, but that is not the answer. The civil servants came, wrote one page and left. Every spring we wait for them to come back. The old man who keeps the records says the state of things was worse in his father's day.","zh":"道路的状况是这里的主要问题。我们国家有了一项关于土地的新法律，行政部门还想再加上三条。我提不出更好的办法：没有什么状态能表达农民在水来时的感受。你可以把损失归因于雨水，可那不是答案。公务员来了，写了一页纸就走了。每年春天我们都等着他们再回来。"},"study":{"tw":[["student",4],["consider",0],["check",3],["research",6],["field",0],["major",3],["think",2],["learn",2]],"en":"I study in the room above the shop. There is one small window and a table full of books. My sister is a student of science; she comes here to research the plants in the field behind the house. We check each other's work every evening. I think this is the only way to learn: consider one thing at a time and then leave it alone. Her major is much harder than mine. My father studied in the same room and never got further than the second book. He says a good table is worth more than a good teacher.","zh":"我在店铺楼上那间屋里学习。屋里只有一扇小窗和一张堆满书的桌子。我妹妹是学理科的学生；她到这里来研究屋后地里的植物。每天晚上我们互相检查作业。我想这是唯一的学习方法：一次只琢磨一件事，然后就放手。她的专业比我的难得多。"},"tie":{"tw":[["draw",0],["ground",3],["finish",2],["marry",0],["join",3],["relate",2],["round",6],["attach",3],["straight",6]],"en":"He wore a black tie to the wedding. The two families will join their names, and after the ceremony they will marry in the old church, on the ground floor of which his mother was born. I had to finish the flowers before nine and attach a card to each one. It is hard to relate one thing to another here. We sat round the table and nobody could draw a straight line. The knot took me ten minutes, and in the photograph it is still crooked. My mother laughed at me and tied it again in one movement.","zh":"他打了条黑领带去参加婚礼。两家人要合成一个姓，仪式之后他们将在那座老教堂里成婚——他母亲就出生在那教堂的底层。我得在九点前把花弄完，并在每一束上别一张卡片。在这里很难把一件事和另一件事联系起来。我们围着桌子坐着，没人能画出一条直线。"},"time":{"tw":[["clock",0],["dead",3],["experience",2],["clip",0],["hour",3],["term",2],["next",6],["sentence",0]],"en":"We have no time, and the clock on the wall is dead. It stopped at five past four one afternoon in June, and nobody has touched it since. Experience tells me the next hour will decide everything. The term ends on Friday, and my last sentence has to be in by then. I will clip the papers together and hand them over at the door. It is the same every year. I have written the date on every page so that I will know the time of it later. Someday someone will read these pages and count the days between them.","zh":"我们没有时间，而墙上的钟是停的。它在六月的一个下午四点零五分停了，此后没人碰过它。经验告诉我，接下来的一个小时会决定一切。学期周五结束，到那时我最后一句必须交上去。我会把纸夹在一起，在门口交出去。每年都是这样。"},"touch":{"tw":[["tactile",4],["concern",0],["catch",3],["act",2],["easy",6],["meet",0],["cover",3],["change",2],["reach",0]],"en":"Do not touch the glass. The tactile map behind it is for blind visitors, and every finger leaves a mark. I have one small concern: the cover of the case is loose. It is easy to change the paper, but you must act before the glue dries. We will meet on Thursday and catch up on the rest. The hand of the woman in the picture is reaching for the same door. The guard watches everybody's hands, and nobody has ever touched the glass twice. He stands there all day and says nothing at all.","zh":"别碰玻璃。后面那张触摸地图是给盲人访客用的，每根手指都会留下印子。我有一个小顾虑：盒子的盖子松了。换纸很容易，但必须在胶干之前动手。我们周四见面，把剩下的部分跟上。画里那个女人的手也正伸向同一扇门。"},"try":{"tw":[["trial",4],["hear",0],["best",3],["act",2],["bring",6],["judge",0],["control",3],["taste",0]],"en":"I will try once more, and then I will stop. The trial next week is about a small house near the river, and the judge has asked me to bring the old papers. We will hear the first witness on Monday. Nothing here is under my control; the best I can do is act quickly and taste the food before I serve it. There is a pain in my back that will not go away. My sister says I should give up, and I tell her that trying is all I have.","zh":"我再试一次，然后就停下。下周的庭审涉及河边一栋小房子，法官要我把旧文件带过去。周一会听第一位证人陈述。这里没有一件事在我掌控之中；我能做的最好的事就是动作快一点，上菜前先尝一口。我背上有一处疼痛怎么也不消。"},"type":{"tw":[["typify",4],["character",0],["breed",3],["write",2],["example",6],["eccentric",0],["shift",3],["adult",2]],"en":"What type of dog is that? The breed is old and rather eccentric: it will typify the whole group in every show. Its character is calm, and the adult dogs sleep all day. I have to write four pages about this type of animal, with an example of each. The night shift begins at ten, and the same man has worked it for years. He says he knows every type by its bark alone. There are forty types in the book, and I have to describe every one of them.","zh":"那是什么品种的狗？这品种很老，也相当古怪：每到比赛它都能代表整组狗的特点。它的性情温和，成年的狗整天睡觉。我得写四页讲这类动物，每一类都要举一个例子。夜班十点开始，同一个人已经干了好几年。他说只听叫声就能认出每一种。"},"use":{"tw":[["usage",4],["employ",0],["apply",0],["drink",3],["demand",2],["require",6],["exercise",0],["board",3],["act",2]],"en":"The use of this room is written on the board. You may employ the machine for two hours a day, but you have to apply in writing first. The usage is strict: no drink near the desk. Older people require a chair and will demand one. We exercise every morning before the doors open, and the act of standing up is the hardest part. Nobody has ever asked me what the machines are for. The man who wrote the rules retired in 1990 and has not been back since. Everyone here knows the rules, and nobody has ever read them.","zh":"这间屋子的用途写在牌子上。你每天可以用这台机器两小时，但得先书面申请。规矩很严：桌边不许喝饮料。年纪大的人需要椅子，而且会开口要。每天早上开门前我们做操，而站起来这个动作是最难的一环。从没有人问过我这些机器是干什么用的。"},"wait":{"tw":[["waiter",4],["expect",3],["extension",3],["act",2],["stay",6],["hold",0],["ambush",3],["look",0]],"en":"We had to wait two hours for a table. The waiter told us to expect another twenty minutes, and then another. My sister could not stay; she had work to do. I left my name at the extension desk and sat in the corner, where I could look at the door. The ambush in the book I was reading lasted three pages. I had to hold the book with both hands, it was so cold. When the table was ready at last, my sister had already gone home. The waiter said the delay was nobody's fault, but every act of service in that place takes an hour.","zh":"我们等位子等了两个小时。服务员说再等二十分钟，然后又二十分钟。我妹妹待不住，她还有活要干。我把名字留在分机台，坐到角落里，从那儿能看见门口。我读的那本书里，一次伏击写了三页。我不得不用两只手抱着书，实在太冷了。"},"wall":{"tw":[["mural",4],["fence",2],["gable",3],["surround",0],["parapet",3],["layer",2],["floor",6],["object",2],["street",6]],"en":"There is a wall around the old garden. On the inside, the mural above the door shows the whole history of the street. The parapet is broken in two places, and a wooden fence covers the gap. Every layer of paint on the wall belongs to a different year. The gable of the house next door leans over it, and on the floor near the gate somebody has left a heavy object. The wall will surround this garden long after we are gone.","zh":"老花园四周有一道墙。墙内侧、门上方那幅壁画讲着这条街的整部历史。墙头有两处塌了，用一道木栅栏挡着缺口。墙上每一层漆都属于不同年份。隔壁房子的山墙朝它倾斜过来，大门附近的地上有人撂下了一个很重的东西。等我们都不在了，这道墙还会围着这座花园。"},"weight":{"tw":[["weighty",4],["burden",0],["load",3],["charge",2],["maximum",6],["bias",2],["excess",6],["angle",0]],"en":"The weight of the box was more than I expected. It is a weighty thing, and the burden of carrying it up the stairs fell on my brother. The maximum load for the old lift is eighty kilos, so we had to go on foot. He put it on the table at an angle and said the charge would be extra. There is a bias in the way we measure these things: two men always say a box is lighter than one man does. The excess goes back to the yard, where the same two men will argue about the angle of the ramp.","zh":"那个箱子比我想的重。它很沉，搬上楼的担子就落在我哥哥身上。这部旧电梯的最大载重是八十公斤，所以我们只好走楼梯。他把箱子斜着放在桌上，说搬运要另收费。我们衡量这些东西时是有偏见的：两个人总说箱子比一个人说的要轻。"},"book":{"tw":[["booking",4],["hold",0],["card",3],["register",2],["novel",6],["record",2],["ticket",3],["essay",6]],"en":"I read one book about the sea every winter. It is not a novel; it is the record of a man who worked on a boat for thirty years. He could not hold a pen at first, so his wife wrote the booking of every trip in a register and kept a ticket from each town they came to. The card inside the cover is my grandfather's, and the essay at the back was written by a schoolboy. Every page is thin and dry, and the words on them have lasted much longer than the boat did.","zh":"每年冬天我都读一本关于海的书。那不是小说，而是一个在船上干了三十年的人的记录。他起初握不住笔，所以他妻子把每次出航的登记都写进一本登记簿，还留下他们到过的每个城镇的船票。封面里那张卡片是我祖父的，后面那篇文章是一个小学生写的。"},"case":{"tw":[["casing",4],["cause",0],["box",3],["problem",2],["trial",6],["slip",0],["face",0],["pack",3]],"en":"In this case there is no easy answer. The problem is not the box; it is the casing inside it, which is thin. Nobody can find the cause. At the trial the judge asked for a slip of paper with the numbers on it, and my face gave me away. I had to pack the whole thing again and take it home on the bus. The next case on the list was even worse. Two weeks later a man came to the door with the same box and asked me the same question again.","zh":"这个案子里没有简单的答案。问题不在箱子，而在里面那层很薄的壳体。没人找得出原因。开审时法官要一张写有数字的纸条，而我的脸色把我出卖了。我只好把东西重新打包，坐公交带回家。清单上的下一个案子更糟。"},"class":{"tw":[["classify",4],["course",0],["count",3],["league",2],["standard",6],["family",0],["rank",6],["form",0]],"en":"Our class has twenty-two children in it. The teacher has to classify them by age and by reading level, and the standard of the older ones is not much higher. We play in a small league on Saturdays, and my rank in the group is fourth. The course lasts one year. The form of the test has changed twice since I came. In my family nobody finished school, so I count myself lucky to be here at all. The teacher says a good class is not a list of names but a habit of working that lasts for years.","zh":"我们班有二十二个孩子。老师得按年龄和阅读水平给他们分类，而大孩子的水平并不高多少。我们周六参加一个小联赛，我在组里的名次是第四。课程为期一年。我入学以来考试的形式已经改过两次。我们家没人读完过中学，所以我觉得自己能在这儿已经很幸运了。"},"country":{"tw":[["rural",4],["land",0],["open",3],["region",2],["nation",0],["state",0],["far",6],["space",3]],"en":"I grew up in the country, in a rural region where the land is cheap and the roads are empty. Our nation has eight such regions, and the state pays for the schools in all of them. The open field behind our house is the only space the children have. The nearest town is far; my aunt says it takes an hour if the wind is against you. In summer the whole country smells of cut grass. The government sends one bus a week, and the driver knows every family in the valley by name.","zh":"我在乡下长大，那是个土地便宜、道路空旷的农业地区。我们国家有八个这样的地区，所有地区的学校都由政府出资。屋后那片开阔的田是孩子们仅有的空间。最近的镇子很远；我姑妈说，要是逆风得走一个小时。夏天整个乡下都是青草被割过的味道。"},"father":{"tw":[["paternal",4],["mother",1],["patriarch",3],["head",2],["grandfather",6],["generate",0],["parent",2],["engender",0]],"en":"My father was born in a house that no longer exists. His paternal grandfather, an old patriarch, was the head of a family of eleven. My mother says the two of them could generate an argument out of nothing, and that noise would engender more noise. Every parent in that street knew everybody else's business. My father never spoke of it, and I only learned the whole story from my aunt. My mother kept a photograph of the old house in a drawer for forty years, and then it was lost.","zh":"我父亲出生在一栋如今已不存在的房子里。他父系那边的祖父，一位老家长，是十一个人大家庭的户主。我母亲说那两个人能凭空吵出一场争论，而那吵闹又会生出更多吵闹。那条街上每对父母都知道别人家的私事。我父亲从不提这些，整个故事我还是从我姑妈那儿听来的。"},"flower":{"tw":[["floral",4],["bloom",0],["bud",3],["develop",2],["tree",6],["prime",0],["daisy",3],["garden",6]],"en":"The flower show opens on the first Saturday of June. Every garden in the village brings something: one rose, one daisy, one strange plant in a pot. The floral tent is the biggest in the county. My aunt watches her buds for weeks; a flower that is not yet in bloom cannot win, and one past its prime cannot either. The tree by the gate develops its leaves late and loses them early. The judge looks at the colour first and the shape last, and he never hurries. The show closes at six and the tent is taken down the same evening.","zh":"花展六月的第一个周六开幕。村里每座园子都拿出点什么：一支玫瑰、一朵雏菊、一盆奇怪的植物。那座花卉帐篷是全县最大的。我姑妈守着花苞看了好几周；还没开的花赢不了，过了盛期的也赢不了。大门边那棵树发芽晚，落叶却早。"},"number":{"tw":[["numeric",4],["square",3],["company",2],["total",3],["count",0],["several",6],["least",6],["bit",0]],"en":"Write your number at the top of the page. The system is numeric: no letters, no dashes. Our company counts every call, and the total last month was a little over nine hundred. Several of them were wrong. A square of paper with the same number is pinned to the board. I am tired, and it takes the least bit of noise to make me lose the count. The office has a number for everything: the door, the phone, the pile of paper on the shelf. I write mine on the back of my hand so that I will not forget it.","zh":"把号码写在页面顶端。格式是纯数字：不要字母，不要短横。我们公司统计每一通电话，上个月的总数略超九百。其中有几通是错的。一张写着同样号码的方纸钉在告示板上。我累了，一点点响声就能让我数乱。"},"school":{"tw":[["scholastic",4],["educate",2],["conservatory",3],["college",6],["train",0],["swim",2],["graduate",6],["civilise",0]],"en":"The school stands at the end of the street. Its scholastic record is not famous, but it has educated half the village. There is a conservatory behind it where the children train in music, and a small pool where they swim in summer. My sister went on to college and will graduate in July. Nobody here speaks of civilising anybody; they only want the children to be able to read. The building is old, and the roof was repaired with money the parents collected themselves. Every year the oldest children repaint the front wall before the summer.","zh":"学校坐落在街的尽头。它的学业成绩并不出名，却教出了半个村子的人。后面有个玻璃琴房，孩子们在那里练音乐；还有个小水池，夏天他们在里面游泳。我妹妹后来上了大学，七月就要毕业。这里没人说什么开化谁，他们只想让孩子能读书。"},"simple":{"tw":[["simplicity",4],["bare",0],["square",3],["complex",1],["perfect",6],["mere",0],["fool",3],["straightforward",6]],"en":"The answer is simple. The plan has a kind of simplicity that fools people: a bare room, one square table, one chair. Any honest worker would call it straightforward. The truth is that it is not complex, and it is not perfect either. It is elementary, and only a fool would try to improve it. My father built the whole thing in a single week, and it still stands. For a mere fifty pounds we could make it better, but nobody wants to spend the money. So we leave it as it is, and it works.","zh":"答案很简单。这个方案有一种会骗人的简洁：一间空屋、一张方桌、一把椅子。任何老实的工人都会说这很直白。事实是它不复杂，也不完美。它很基础，只有傻子才会想去改进它。我父亲用一周就把它全做出来了，而它至今还立在那儿。"},"space":{"tw":[["spatial",4],["blank",0],["hole",3],["distance",0],["infinite",0],["shuttle",6],["key",3],["earth",6]],"en":"There is no space left in the cupboard. A hole in the wall behind it gives us a little more, and the distance from there to the window is about a metre. In the city the shuttle bus comes every ten minutes. My teacher says space is infinite and the earth is not, and then he draws a blank on the board. The key to the whole problem is spatial: it is about where things are, not what they are.","zh":"柜子里没地方了。它后面墙上的一个洞给了我们一点余地，从那儿到窗户的距离大约一米。在城里，穿梭巴士每十分钟一班。我老师说空间是无限的，而地球不是，然后他在黑板上画了个空白。整个问题的关键在于空间：它关乎东西在哪里，而不是它们是什么。"},"suppose":{"tw":[["supposition",4],["guess",0],["suspect",3],["assume",2],["premise",3],["presume",6],["imagine",0],["say",0]],"en":"I suppose you have heard the story. It is a supposition, nothing more; nobody can say where it began. I suspect the first man only wanted to make us guess. Do not assume that the premise is true, and do not presume that I know either. Imagine a village where nobody had ever left, and you will understand why the story grew. That is the whole of it. I have told it to my children exactly as it was told to me, without adding anything. They will tell it to theirs, and the supposition will be the same.","zh":"我猜这个故事你听过。它只是一个推测，仅此而已；没人说得出它从哪儿开始。我怀疑最初那个人只是想让我们猜。别认定那个前提是真的，也别以为我就知道。想一想一个从没有人离开过的村子，你就会明白这故事为什么会越传越大。事情就是这样。"},"term":{"tw":[["terminal",4],["condition",0],["subject",3],["word",2],["current",6],["terminus",0],["predicate",3],["quantity",2]],"en":"The term ends in three weeks. In this subject the predicate carries most of the meaning, and one wrong word can change the whole sentence. The quantity of reading is small; the interest is not. I stand at the bus terminal every morning and watch the current of people go past. The line stops at a terminus two streets from my house, and the condition of the road there is terrible. My father uses the same word for the season, the school and the length of a loan. He says a word is only a tool, and a tool should be used more than once.","zh":"学期还有三周就结束了。在这门学科里，谓语承载了大部分意思，一个用错的词就能改变整句。阅读量不大，趣味性却不少。每天早上我站在公交总站看人流经过。这条线路的终点站离我家两条街，而那里路况糟透了。"},"wild":{"tw":[["wilderness",4],["crazy",0],["barren",3],["tame",1],["fish",6],["waste",0],["bird",6],["furious",0]],"en":"The garden has gone wild again. Beyond the fence there is a piece of wilderness where no bird has nested for years and the ground is barren. My neighbour is furious about the waste of good land, and he says only a crazy man would leave it like that. His own cat is tame and fat. I go there to fish in the small stream and to be alone for an hour. In spring the stream is full of small fish and the birds come back to the fence. Nobody in the village has walked to the far end of it for years.","zh":"园子又野了。栅栏那边有一片荒地，多年没有鸟在这里筑巢，土地贫瘠。我邻居对这么好的一块地被浪费感到愤怒，他说只有疯子才会让它这样。他自己那只猫又温顺又肥。我去那里的小溪里钓鱼，独自待上一个小时。"},"act":{"tw":[["begin",3],["serve",2],["refrain",1],["move",0],["deal",3],["event",2],["order",6],["play",0]],"en":"The act begins at seven. First they serve the soup, then the play starts, and nobody may move from their seat. I have to deal with the last table and give the order to the kitchen before the second act. Please refrain from talking during the music. The whole event lasts two hours, and by the end my feet are dead. The same thing happens every Friday, and I still enjoy it. The young woman who plays the mother has never acted before, and she is very good. After the last curtain we wash the glasses and count the money.","zh":"这幕戏七点开始。先上汤，然后戏才开演，谁都不许离开座位。我得收拾最后一张桌子，并在第二幕之前把点单送进厨房。音乐响起时请勿交谈。整个活动持续两小时，结束时我的脚都站麻了。每周五都是这样，而我依然挺喜欢。"},"add":{"tw":[["bring",0],["subtract",1],["combine",6],["total",0],["include",3],["count",2],["extra",6],["contribute",0]],"en":"Please add these two figures and bring me the total. You may not subtract anything, and you must include the extra charge for delivery. If you combine the two lists, the count will be wrong by one. Everyone in the office had to contribute a little. I checked it twice before I took it in, and the answer looked simple to everybody. The figures come from two different books, and each one has its own way of counting. If the total is not the same in both, we start again from the beginning.","zh":"请把这两个数字加起来，把总数拿来给我。不许减掉任何一项，还必须把额外的运费算进去。如果把两张清单合并，计数就会差一个。办公室里每个人都得出一点力。我交上去之前核了两遍，而在所有人看来答案都显而易见。"},"agree":{"tw":[["check",0],["accept",2],["disagree",1],["consider",6],["fit",0],["meet",3],["suit",2],["negotiate",6]],"en":"I agree with you about the price, but I cannot accept the date. We can meet on Thursday and negotiate the rest. Let me check the small room first; if the table does not fit, the whole plan is no good. Consider the other offer before you decide. My brother disagrees with me and says the later date would suit him much better. He wants the later date because his son will be home from the army by then. That is a good reason, and I have no good reason of my own.","zh":"价钱上我同意你，但日期我不能接受。我们周四见面，其余的事再谈。先让我看看那间小屋；桌子放不下的话，整个计划就不行。做决定前你也考虑一下另一个报价。我哥哥不同意我，他说晚一点那个日期对他合适得多。"},"allow":{"tw":[["admit",3],["accept",2],["deny",1],["require",6],["trust",3],["assign",2],["enable",6],["grant",0]],"en":"They do not allow dogs in the shop. The sign says they cannot admit animals, and they deny that it has anything to do with the owner. Anyone who wants to bring one must accept the rule. The job will require an hour of training, and the manager will assign somebody to help you. This small key will enable you to open the back door. I trust they will grant us one more week. The shop next door allows them, and half the street goes there instead. The owner says he will not change his mind, and I believe him.","zh":"他们不许带狗进店。牌子上说不能接纳动物，他们否认这与主人有关。想带狗来的人必须接受这条规矩。这份活需要一小时培训，经理会指派一个人帮你。这把小钥匙能让你打开后门。我相信他们会再宽限我们一周。"},"answer":{"tw":[["reply",2],["field",3],["meet",2],["question",1],["serve",3],["counter",3],["state",2],["result",0]],"en":"I wrote my answer and put it on the counter. There was no reply for a week, and then a short letter came. The state of the field is the real question here: nobody can meet in a wet meadow, and the result would be a mess. I asked again at the second window, and the woman there could not serve me either. So I went home and waited for the third letter. In the third week I met the owner himself at the door of the office. He answered every question except the one I had actually asked.","zh":"我把答案写好放在柜台上。一周都没有回音，然后来了一封短信。这里的真正问题是场地状况：没人能在湿草地里集会，结果只会一团糟。我又到第二个窗口去问，那里的女士也帮不了我。于是我回家等第三封信。"},"bottom":{"tw":[["bed",0],["base",3],["hit",2],["side",2],["spot",6],["behind",0],["foot",3],["land",2],["plate",6]],"en":"At the bottom of the garden there is a bed of stones. The base of the old wall is under it, and on the far side you can see a plate of iron fixed into the ground. We used to hit it with a stick when we were children. The spot behind the tree is where my dog liked to sleep. From there you can put your foot on the land beyond the fence. In summer the whole garden smells of wet stone, and the bed under the wall is the coolest place in it.","zh":"园子最底下有一片石头地。那堵旧墙的基座就在下面，靠外的一侧能看到一块嵌进地里的铁板。我们小时候常拿棍子敲它。树后那一处是我家狗爱睡的地方。从那儿你可以把脚伸到栅栏外的土地上去。"},"break":{"tw":[["blow",3],["change",2],["repair",1],["check",0],["chip",3],["dance",2],["die",0],["back",6]],"en":"Take a break at four; you look tired. A single blow from that hammer can chip the stone, and the break in the wall will only get worse. Nobody can repair it in one day, and a small change here will not help. Check the back of the house first, where the wind comes in. The old tree will die this year. Come and dance with me instead; the wall has waited thirty years. The crack runs from the window down to the floor, and in winter it lets the cold air in.","zh":"四点歇一下吧，你看上去累了。那把锤子敲一下就能把石头崩出缺口，而墙上的裂口只会越来越大。一天之内谁也修不好，在这里做点小改动也没用。先去查看房子背面，风是从那儿灌进来的。那棵老树今年会死。不如过来跟我跳舞吧，那堵墙等了三十年了。"},"change":{"tw":[["alter",0],["break",3],["dress",2],["stay",1],["exchange",0],["cut",3],["travel",2],["reason",6],["shift",0]],"en":"You cannot change this without asking. Nothing can alter the size of the door, and if you cut the frame you will break the glass. There is a good reason for the rule: the shift of the wind in winter is strong enough to travel through any small gap. I had to dress in two coats and stay inside. In the future we will exchange the old panes for new ones. Anything you alter in this room has to be written in the book by the door. The book has been there for a hundred years and the handwriting is very small.","zh":"不打招呼你不能改动这里。门的尺寸无法更改，要是削了框子就会打碎玻璃。这条规定有它的道理：冬天风向一变，风大得能从任何小缝里钻进来。我不得不穿上两件外套待在屋里。以后我们会把旧玻璃换成新的。"},"clean":{"tw":[["clear",0],["wash",3],["change",2],["dirty",1],["enough",6],["fair",5],["brush",3],["remove",2],["water",6],["fresh",0]],"en":"Keep the room clean: wash the floor, brush the table and remove every plate before you leave. The water in the bucket must be clear, not fresh, and the cloth has to be clean enough to use twice. If the sheets are dirty, change them. It is not fair to leave that work to the next person. I have done it for eleven years, and the room has never once been dirty on my shift. When the shift ends I put the brushes back in the cupboard and lock it. The next person will find everything exactly where it belongs.","zh":"把屋子保持干净：走之前擦地、刷桌、把所有盘子收走。桶里的水要清，不必是新打的；抹布得干净到还能再用一次。床单脏了就换。把活儿留给下一个人是不公平的。我干了十一年，我班上这屋子从没脏过。"},"comfort":{"tw":[["ease",0],["calm",3],["aid",2],["discomfort",1],["sense",6],["console",0],["relief",3],["condition",2]],"en":"The old chair gives me more comfort than the new one. It has a calm shape and a soft cushion, and when my back is bad it is a real aid. The discomfort in my knees goes away within a minute of sitting down. My only sense of relief in the evening comes from that chair. My sister tries to console me by saying it is an ordinary chair, but she does not have to sit in it all day. For ease of mind I have written its condition on a card and hung the card on the back of the chair.","zh":"那把旧椅子比新的更让我舒服。它形制沉静、坐垫柔软，我背痛的时候它真帮得上忙。一坐下不到一分钟，膝盖的不适就消失了。晚上我唯一的放松感就来自那把椅子。我妹妹想安慰我，说那只是把普通的椅子，可她不用整天坐在上面。"},"continue":{"tw":[["cover",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["discontinue",1],["bring",6],["stay",0],["cross",3],["talk",2],["extend",0],["move",6]],"en":"We will continue the work tomorrow. Nobody can carry on like this: two of the men have gone home and the rain shows no sign of stopping. Every act of repair here begins in the rain. If they discontinue the service, we will have to cover the roof ourselves and stay until it is done. I cannot talk about it any longer. Let us cross the yard, move the boxes inside, and then we will extend the plan by a week. Somebody has to bring the tarpaulin before the night shift starts.","zh":"明天我们继续干。没人能这样撑下去：两个人已经回家了，雨也没有要停的样子。这里每一次修理都是在雨里开的头。要是他们停掉这项服务，我们就得自己盖屋顶，一直干完为止。我不能再聊这个了。我们穿过院子，把箱子搬进屋，然后把这个计划延长一周。"}}});
